["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-5550f44bceaa672f86efc6c5d04c10cd50f63e437de126a49ac4b7c2b58eda0d","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"# A stage left by a killed process is removed\n\n## Outcome\n\nA `planning.aep-stage-*` directory left by a process that was killed during publication is removed the next time\na publication runs, without ever removing a stage another live process owns.\n\n## Why\n\naep#40 removes a stage on every error return and on unwinding, but a killed process runs no destructor. Its stage\nstays beside the projection: recovery re-renders into a fresh directory and never removes the old one (test\n`a_stage_a_killed_process_left_does_not_stop_recovery_and_is_not_removed`). Stage names carry pid and counter\n(`stage_directory()`), which is what a sweep can test for liveness, with the pid-namespace caveat the aep#40\nadversary noted.\n","status":"draft","title":"A stage left by a killed process is removed"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/a-killed-publication-stage-is-swept"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-7fe0fe35f338a0a43a7f59e1ba345671@1"],"audit":["aud-21e1e313c27982f5412181fe455ae106"],"command_id":"cmd-child-5550f44bceaa672f86efc6c5d04c10cd50f63e437de126a49ac4b7c2b58eda0d","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-21e1e013c2797ddc412180fe455adf53"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-5550f44bceaa672f86efc6c5d04c10cd50f63e437de126a49ac4b7c2b58eda0d","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","record_id":"aep.applied:child-5550f44bceaa672f86efc6c5d04c10cd50f63e437de126a49ac4b7c2b58eda0d@1~1edd1d4a96e50ce3","recorded_at":"2026-09-26T01:09:42Z"},"subject":["aep.